{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T09:17:27.180Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7687d94a08e852f40579b9f7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-http-33ck"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Distinguish exact serialized byte costs from heuristic token estimates in difference packets"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-http#5 (filed 2026-10-29, missed by the blind issue watch). src/core.ts computes tokens(value) as ceil(max(JSON, TOON UTF-8 bytes)/4) and reports it as estimatedTokens with its budget; the epic's bounded-difference-packet contract is met, but agent consumers cannot distinguish an enforceable serialized-byte ceiling from an approximate model-token cost (ceil(bytes/4) is neither a tokenizer count nor a guaranteed upper bound). Request: expose the exact packet byte costs alongside the estimate, and name the estimator explicitly in receipts/docs so a context budget claim cannot be read as a measured token count. Static proposal; no transport defect reproduced."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["api","gh:unbraind/pm-http#5","measurement"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:17:27.180Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:17:27.180Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"543e8cd39f9afc2ccbeccb817ac4bd73838bf3c3962e0c887fc208f2f6ed1db9","item_hash_version":3,"messa